From e77e6a1e179f2bc592d865fb41fc2e96f5662e04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 11:07:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 427/572] fix(st-rif): do not assign an unused value for node
 when parsing config

In risaf_parse_fwconfig(), node was assigned a -1 value. But it is then
overwritten without the first value being used. Remove this assignment.
This issue was found by Coverity: Defect (unused_value).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 3f09cde612d373015491e5e4651b8be493b1aa8e fix(st-rif): do not assign an unused value for node when parsing config]
Change-Id: Id463d91bb62e37e3413ee8ddd9089f7a93c8e8b0
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/545601
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/st/rif/stm32mp2_risaf.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/st/rif/stm32mp2_risaf.c b/drivers/st/rif/stm32mp2_risaf.c
index b180e287c6..cef6eda1e9 100644
--- a/drivers/st/rif/stm32mp2_risaf.c
+++ b/drivers/st/rif/stm32mp2_risaf.c
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 /*
- * Copyright (c) 2025, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
+ * Copyright (c) 2025-2026, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
  *
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
  */
@@ -606,7 +606,7 @@ static int risaf_parse_fwconfig(uintptr_t config)
 {
 	struct stm32mp2_risaf_platdata *pdata = &stm32mp2_risaf;
 	unsigned int i;
-	int node = -1;
+	int node;
 	int subnode;
 	const void *fdt = (const void *)config;
 	const char *compatible_str = "st,stm32mp2-mem-firewall";
-- 
